laurel 2006: USB gadget starts from STARTUP(EARLY_BOOT) (kernel_bootstrap_thread, before IOKit matching ends and bsd_init) in raw-frame mode (the panic engine: ARP by hand, console ring from byte 0 as UDP 5140, commands on UDP 5141 incl. panic); bsd_init attaches ue0 after net_init_run (laurel_usb_net_attach) and the socket log goes on at the raw position. sweet_cpu_mark_offline also clears cpu_running and sets SIGPdisabled so cross-calls never wait on a half-started core.
